  "title": "CHAPTER 1: HISTORY OF PUNJAB",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "yu73nm6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient Punjab"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Punjab developed through the Indus Valley Civilization, Vedic Period, Persian and Greek Invasions, and Mauryan Empire.",
        "Medieval Punjab was dominated by the Delhi Sultanate (1206–1526) and the Mughal Empire (1526–1739).",
        "The Sikh Period features the Ten Sikh Gurus, the Foundation of Khalsa in 1699, Sikh Misls (1716–1799), and Ranjit Singh's Sikh Empire (1799–1849).",
        "Following the Anglo-Sikh Wars, Punjab came under British Rule from 1849 until Indian Independence in 1947."
      ],
      "id": "6mei71q"
    },
